          "filename": "110326-N-HI707-303 (5571298585).jpg",
          "caption": "U.S. Navy Boatswain's Mate 3rd Class Anthony Woo waits for a bucket of paint to be lowered March 26, 2011, aboard the frigate USS Robert G. Bradley (FFG 49), while moored in Port Gentil, Gabon, in support of Africa Partnership Station (APS) West. APS is an international security cooperation initiative facilitated by Commander, U.S. Naval Forces Europe-Africa aimed at strengthening global maritime partnerships through training and collaborative activities in order to improve maritime safety and security in Africa. (DoD photo by Mass Communication Specialist 1st Class Darryl Wood, U.S. Navy/Released)",
